---
import Video from "../ProjectVideo.astro";
import Figure from "../ProjectFigure.astro";
import Playback from "../ProjectPlayback.astro";
import "../../styles/architected.css";
const questions = [
  { title: "Material meets construction", text: "Geometry must serve its intended function while accommodating fabrication and robotic handling.", path: "m12 25 20-11 20 11-20 11ZM12 25v23l20 11 20-11V25M32 36v23M22 20l20 11M22 31v22M42 31v22" },
  { title: "Connections define access", text: "A joint needs a feasible approach, accessible grasping locations, and appropriate assembly tolerances.", path: "M9 36h17v7h12v-7h17v20H9ZM23 5h18v18H23ZM32 23v12m-6-6 6 6 6-6" },
  { title: "Every placement changes the next", text: "Repeated assembly must account for alignment, workspace access, and previously placed components.", path: "M5 38h17v18H5Zm19 0h17v18H24Zm19 0h17v18H43ZM43 8h17v18H43ZM13 31V17h22m-6-6 6 6-6 6M51 27v7" },
];
const operations = ["Grasp", "Lift & transport", "Align above", "Insert vertically", "Release", "Repeat"];
---
<section class="architected-hero" id="module-demo" aria-labelledby="project-title">
  <div class="architected-hero-intro"><h1 id="project-title">Design and Robotic Assembly <br /> of Architected Structures</h1><p>Connecting material architecture, modular interfaces, and robotic assembly to advance adaptable infrastructure.</p></div>
  <Video id="structures-families" hero credits />
  <p id="media-status" class="sr-only" role="status"></p>
</section>
<div class="architected-content">
  <section class="architected-section" id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
    <div class="architected-heading"><p class="architected-stage">Problem</p><div><h2 id="problem-title">How can complex materials<br /> become buildable structures?</h2><p>Geometry can shape a material’s structural and environmental functions. Building with it brings fabrication, connections, handling, and assembly into the same design problem.</p></div></div>
    <div class="architected-questions">{questions.map(q => <article><svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" width="64" height="64" aria-hidden="true"><path d={q.path} fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round" /></svg><h3>{q.title}</h3><p>{q.text}</p></article>)}</div>
  </section>
  <section class="architected-section" id="innovations" aria-labelledby="innovations-title">
    <div class="architected-heading"><p class="architected-stage">Innovations &amp; solutions</p><div><h2 id="innovations-title">Co-design the module,<br /> the joint, and the motion.</h2></div></div>
    <article class="architected-strand" id="material-design" aria-labelledby="material-title">
      <div class="architected-strand-copy"><span class="architected-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3 id="material-title">Architected material<br /> and module design</h3><p>Explore how porosity and internal architecture shape modular components. Bring functional design, manufacturability, and robotic accessibility together from the beginning.</p></div>
      <div class="architected-material-pair"><div><h4>Module concept</h4><Figure id="module" quiet linked={false} /></div><div><h4>Fabrication reference</h4><Figure id="manufacturing" quiet linked={false} /></div></div>
    </article>
    <article class="architected-strand architected-joint" id="joint-demo" aria-labelledby="joint-title">
      <div class="architected-strand-copy"><span class="architected-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3 id="joint-title">Assembly-oriented<br /> connection design</h3><p>Joint geometry defines how components approach, align, and engage. Study insertion directions alongside structural requirements and manufacturing tolerances.</p></div>
      <Video id="structures-joint" credits />
    </article>
    <div class="architected-connections"><h4>Connection-design concepts</h4><Figure id="connections" quiet linked={false} /></div>
    <article class="architected-planning" id="planning" aria-labelledby="planning-title">
      <div class="architected-planning-head"><span class="architected-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3 id="planning-title">Robotic assembly<br /> planning and execution</h3><p>Study the sequence from grasp to release. Virtual environments expose workspace and motion constraints; sensing, contact-aware manipulation, and verification are the next research steps.</p></div>
      <ol class="architected-operations" aria-label="Illustrated vertical-insertion workflow">{operations.map((operation,i) => <li><span aria-hidden="true">0{i+1}</span><strong>{operation}</strong>{i<operations.length-1 && <span class="architected-operation-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>}</li>)}</ol>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="architected-section" id="demonstrations" aria-labelledby="demo-title">
    <div class="architected-heading"><p class="architected-stage">Research demonstrations</p><div><h2 id="demo-title">From one placement<br /> to a growing structure.</h2><p>Prescribed assembly motions make the relationship between geometry and sequence visible. Physical validation of gripping, contact, tolerances, and connection performance remains a research priority.</p></div></div>
    <div id="assembly-demo"><Video id="structures-assembly" credits /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="architected-section" id="application" aria-labelledby="application-title">
    <div class="architected-application"><div><p class="architected-stage">Application</p><h2 id="application-title">Modular coastal<br /> infrastructure.</h2><p>NACRE coastal modules, within the broader AMERICA research effort, connect coastal and ecological design objectives with fabrication, connection, and construction.</p><p>This application provides practical questions for robot-assisted handling and placement—and for future evaluation.</p></div><Figure id="breakwater" quiet linked={false} /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="architected-collaboration" id="collaborate" aria-labelledby="collaborate-title"><div><p class="architected-stage">Research team &amp; collaborators</p><h2 id="collaborate-title">Build across disciplines.</h2></div><div><p>Material architecture · Fabrication · Robotics<br /> Structural &amp; coastal engineering · Ecology</p></div></section>
</div>
<Playback />
